# Versioned decoder-training integration plan

Version 3.553. Updated 2026-11-27 with registered transport scope and capacity checks.

Status. Both saved T5 policy candidates reached the output cap on every fictional held-out row. In the later matched Qwen2.5 comparison, model-reported loss fell on the three fixed TRAIN rows and exact held-out output remained 0/3 at both checkpoints. The four-teacher study, independent source-fidelity evaluation and cross-architecture measurements remain open.

Coordination workaround: the user asked this automated system to make progress around the dependency block. One independent metadata-contract candidate has now been built and locally tested outside the submodule: [candidate and handoff](/tmp/decoder-contract-candidate-20261120-fhz39b46/README.md), [code](/tmp/decoder-contract-candidate-20261120-fhz39b46/contract_shapes.py), [30-test result summary](/tmp/decoder-contract-candidate-20261120-fhz39b46/result-summary.json). It uses the frozen proposed schema and synthetic fixtures, with no project imports, model loads, Source leases, project/Git writes or new resource owner. This is concrete candidate engineering progress, not canonical integration or scientific qualification.

## Objective and authority

Scope: the entire world legal corpus → source-grounded LegalIR → Lean 4,
across jurisdictions and original source languages; the U.S. Code is a pilot.
Preserve original source bytes/spans, provenance, edition/revision,
applicability, interpretation and definition identities. Compare complete
typed-AST/source-faithfulness and Lean compilation/kernel results separately
on matched source/dependency-grouped cohorts, permitted context and
compute/inference budgets. Report coverage, pending/unsupported/abstained
counts and metric denominators by jurisdiction, language and edition.
Pending-review source-faithfulness stays unknown: include these cases in
coverage, outside source-faithfulness accuracy denominators.

Integrate mechanistic interpretability, bounded experimental weight-space programming, and reinforcement-learning credit assignment into the existing legal-autoformalization decoder training loop. Reuse versioned modules across decoder architectures and sizes through explicit capability adapters. Compare spaCy8D, GTE-small384D, multilingual-GTE768D, and Leanstral4096D supervision without assuming equivalent semantic spaces or arbitrary dimension conversion.

Optimize total measured compute and wall time to a predefined held-out source-faithfulness threshold, subject to formal-validity and retention requirements. Report methods that fail to reach the threshold. Lower loss, improved probes, syntax validity, successful compilation, and high reward are distinct observations; none substitutes for legal source correspondence.

The original objective remains in the immutable [attachment](/home/barberb/.codex/attachments/198ce801-199a-411b-85de-228dde81e251/pasted-text-1.txt). The user subsequently authorized read-only research in the submodule. This plan does not authorize project changes, model imports, installation, new CI callers, training, or resource-budget changes. All future validation is local; do not dispatch GitHub Actions. Preserve original receipts, checkpoints, failures, charges, legal-review requirements, and existing owner custody.

