## 1. Build on the existing stack

Repository research found the missing work in `ipfs_datasets_py`; no new training supervisor or competing registry is needed.

| Responsibility | Existing owner | Integration boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Reviewed pretrained training/generation | `optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer/autoencoder_training_worker.py` | `TorchReviewedDecoderBackend`, reviewed job specifications and caller-owned runtime guards |
| Compact learned source384 sequence decoder | `logic/formalization/autoencoder/source_training_v2.py` | Existing train/runtime/evaluate/load APIs and pinned donor semantics |
| Fixed-schema scalar decoder | `logic/formalization/autoencoder/structured_source_384.py` | Preserve explicit grammar/array/class limitations |
| Same-codec distillation | `decoder_distillation_experiment.py` | Existing private CE plus detached-teacher KL baseline; no implied teacher qualification |
| Cross-width warm start | `gte_decoder_warm_start.py`, `gte_decoder_transfer_replay.py` | Exact donor copy plus new input boundary; preparation/replay is not completed KD |
| Masked representation learning | `alignment_masked_contrastive.py`, `alignment_relation_mask_handoff.py` | Existing masks, relation review and source/context binding |
| Gradient diagnostics | `long_span_gradient_trace_training.py`, `decoder_gradient_replay.py` | Exact committed-step replay before approximate attribution; private diagnostic backward passes |
| Retention and proof feedback | `legal_span_mixed_replay.py`, `trusted_feedback_trainer.py`, `legal_ir_proof_feedback_replay.py` | Existing pool/optimizer state, deduplication, current-proof eligibility and holdout protection |
| Sparse update transport | `modal_autoencoder_patch_codec.py` | Typed compatible sparse postimages; not a generic dense Torch delta format |
| Checkpoints and promotion | `logic/formalization/checkpoints.py` | Existing manifests, domains, lifecycle and provenance |

Names without a package prefix are expanded in the research report. Source inspection establishes responsibilities, not fresh runtime qualification of every API.

The reviewed Torch backend actually supports declared encoder-decoder and causal-LM routes, injected model/optimizer/tokenizer, finite gradient/clipping checks, generation and checkpoint/optimizer/RNG handling. Other architecture families and capabilities require explicit adapters and conformance evidence.

`logic/intent_ir/decoder.py` is a wire parser/migrator, not the neural trainer. Reuse it only where Intent IR is the declared output format. Intent IR is not automatically LegalIR or a proof of source meaning.

## 2. Four separate teacher contracts

| Lane | Source-established contract | Remaining selected-run binding |
|---|---|---|
| spaCy8D | Linguistic feature hashing into8 buckets, L2 normalization, six-decimal rounding; explicit legacy blank-en and local `en_core_web_sm` profiles | Exact backend, pipeline/package/codec identity and observation provenance |
| GTE-small384D | `thenlper/gte-small@17e1f347d17fe144873b1201da91788898c639cd`; receipt profile mean pooling/L2/CPU-float32/512-token reject-overlength | Authenticate chosen local assets, input receipts, source selectors and runtime profile |
| Multilingual-GTE768D | `Alibaba-NLP/gte-multilingual-base@9bbca17d9273fd0d03d5725c7a4b0f6b45142062`; code `Alibaba-NLP/new-impl@40ced75c3017eb27626c9d4ea981bde21a2662f4`; CLS/L2/CPU-float32/8192-token reject-overlength | Exact selected assets/code and producer receipts |
| Leanstral4096D | Existing `Leanstral-1.5-119B-A6B-NVFP4.gguf` profile; declared SHA256 `4668fd2a6d2764de250489852230e96238eb5c0d7495866eb3b9c6c4fac5c7da`; last pooling/L2/512 tokens | Existing operation-bound native full-forward owner, complete selected asset verification, resources and closure |

These are inspected source contracts, not a claim that assets were loaded or admitted in this research. The separate older Leanstral discovery-only route remains closed; it must not be confused with the existing full-forward owner.

SpaCy8 coordinates are hash buckets with collisions, not eight independently named semantic features. The source384 model's internal8D residual branch is another representation: its384D skip connection is required. Equal widths do not establish equivalent semantics.

Evaluate each teacher independently in three roles: inference-time conditioning, training-only distillation, and retrieval. Preserve original source bytes/spans and permitted governing context. Introduce selective fusion only after showing complementary development errors. Keep separate projectors, availability contracts, teacher dropout, missing-teacher behavior and disagreement diagnostics.

Do not arbitrarily truncate vectors, relabel a768-to384 adapted latent as GTE-small, or infer native embeddings from a model's advertised hidden width. Nested representations require an explicitly validated producer/training contract.

## 3. Portable interfaces with explicit capabilities

Map logical contracts onto existing owners before introducing new types:

- Model adapter: generate, score actions, supervised training, policy training, observe/intervene on activations, enumerate update targets, apply reversible updates.
- Teacher/conditioning profiles: exact producer and input identities, layout/dtype/normalization, fit population, projections, train/inference availability and permitted uses.
- Trajectory: behavior checkpoint, sampling/masks, actions and probabilities when supported, output/AST alignment uncertainty, termination and cost.
- Independent evaluation: structural, semantic, source, formal, abstention and retention evidence with unknown/error/unsupported states.
- Credit record: observed reward, learned predictions, named advantage estimator, counterfactual effects and attribution diagnostics as separate fields.
- Update proposal: exact parent/tensor targets/delta, motivating evidence, optimizer treatment, rollback and acceptance.

Unsupported and unverified are different from supported. Generation-only models cannot enter policy algorithms requiring probabilities. Recurrent, state-space, fixed-output and nonautoregressive models retain their own state/action/objective semantics. No universal convergence or zero-effort portability claim follows from a shared interface.

## 4. Training objectives and data boundaries

Keep source-to-complete-LegalIR supervised learning as the foundation. Preserve full targets, EOS, padding/label semantics, source grouping and reviewed or explicitly fictional status.

The existing development owner already implements same-codec CE plus KL from detached teacher logits under identical reference prefixes. Reuse it as the logit-distillation baseline. Embedding-only teachers require feature or relational losses; they do not provide token probabilities.

For feature distillation, use compatible projections and an explicit frozen/stop-gradient target. Fit projection statistics on allowed training groups only. A jointly moving target needs a separate anchored objective and collapse controls. Measure downstream fidelity independently of the alignment loss.

Reuse the existing masked multi-positive objective: known correspondences, incompatible interpretations, analogies and unknown relationships remain distinct. Unknown pairs are not automatic negatives. Preserve jurisdiction, edition, source, interpretation and definition versions.

Teacher forcing and reference-prefix diagnostics are legitimate training tools but must not become hidden inference context. Leanstral hidden-state extraction and generated demonstrations are separate arms. Generated IR/proofs remain candidates until independent source/legal and formal requirements are met.

## 5. Mechanistic interpretability

Start from recorded failures, not a search for attractive circuits. Larger-width source-head experiments show correct raw actor/action/modality/object readouts can coexist with generated action substitutions. Existing gradient replay records token-dominated spikes around a curriculum transition.

Use the existing captured-event infrastructure to establish exact model/Adam/RNG/batch/clipping replay before approximate diagnostics. Current replay has alpha0 and frozen-projection constraints; different losses require a new explicit event profile and parity qualification.

Then test registered hypotheses with source-semantic pairs: actor changes, must/may, exceptions, scope, cardinality and temporal distinctions. Separate probes from causal interventions. Require no-op/sham, matched random, heldout and unrelated-facet controls; check out-of-distribution activation effects.

Transfer semantic tasks and intervention protocols across architectures, not neuron IDs. Interpretability-guided example or parameter selection must beat equal-budget controls on independent fidelity/retention. Probe accuracy, attribution magnitude and gradient cosine are not acceptance criteria.

## 6. Weight-space programming

Treat programmatic edits as a bounded proposal mechanism, not the primary method for rewriting large model weights. Begin with teacher/input projectors, small routing/ranking modules, semantic heads and compatible decoder/LoRA adapters.

Use existing exact donor-copy/new-boundary initialization and donor replay as baselines. Compare proposed edits against supervised updates, matched random edits and applicable explicit rules under equal proposal-selection budgets.

Every proposal binds checkpoint ancestry, exact tensor names/shapes/dtypes/ties, precision/quantization handling, edit procedure, constraints, optimizer-state treatment, rollback and results. Dense edits cannot silently use a sparse codec. No old optimizer moments transfer without compatibility evidence.

Keep accepted parents unchanged while evaluating isolated candidates. Rejected proposals remain recorded costs. Transfer procedures and hypotheses between architectures, not arbitrary raw tensor deltas.

## 7. Reinforcement learning and credit assignment

Separate credit over output decisions, training-example allocation and parameter updates. Mechanistic attribution is not automatically a valid advantage estimator.

Progress through supervised diagnostics, justified preference training, an outcome-policy baseline, and only then finer credit. DPO is a preference baseline; a declared PPO/GRPO/other policy route requires actual behavior-policy/action-probability support. Existing proof-feedback updates are not by themselves policy-gradient RL.

Preserve an independent reward vector: structure, actors/arguments, modality, conditions/exceptions, time/cardinality, definitions/source correspondence, formal validity, abstention and cost. Training scalarization is versioned; proof success cannot offset a mistranslation for admission. Unknown legal meaning stays unknown.

Fine-grained experiments can use verified facets, controlled alternatives, repair trajectories and learned return prediction. Record assumptions, uncertainty, residuals, group composition and off-policy handling. RUDDER-style redistribution or potential shaping requires its own return/terminal consistency contract; neither guarantees useful causal credit here.

Keep current proof eligibility, trusted-feedback deduplication, holdout exclusions and compatible mixed replay. Compiler outcomes are discrete verification signals, not differentiable gradients.

## 8. Historical baselines that the new plan must beat fairly

The research records distinct experiments, not one cumulative qualification:

| Historical scope | Recorded observation | Limit |
|---|---|---|
| Early gradient-spike study |0/48 exact validation paragraphs; exact selected-event replay | Not the latest output frontier or a proved causal mechanism |
| Later generated-field study |768D final candidates42/48 exact; every2 candidate41/48; all18 fits select epoch0 | Repeatedly exposed authored development panels; changed auxiliary exposure; no promotion |
| Source-head learning-rate follow-up |Two384D final candidates47/48;768D candidates46/48 and45/48 | Stronger final attempts still fail acceptance; selected states differ; guardian cleanup failure retained |

The source-head768D/2718 run selects epoch52 with14/48 exact and161 missing rules. Do not report its45/48 final attempt as the selected checkpoint. Earlier zero-ready768 preparation does not mean later768D numerical fits did not happen.

The repeated48 cases across widths/seeds are not independent holdout populations. Fixed-update timings are not equal-compute convergence. Rate changes also affect AdamW shrinkage; standalone probes and full decoders have different exposure and clipping.

Preserve acceptance gates and report the full coverage/error/cost frontier. A prospectively revised development selector needs its own version and review; it cannot retrofit legal admission or silently promote historical candidates.

## 9. Experiment sequence and feasibility gates

Before optimizing, check the complete effective input after preprocessing, including source/context/teacher/prefix information. Identical observable inputs with incompatible required meanings need additional context or an explicit accepted-output-set contract. Embedding collisions alone do not prove impossibility when raw text is available; distinct vectors do not prove a finite head will learn them.

Verify that the selected grammar, codec and output budget express the entire norm. Do not discard clauses to fit a smaller model.

| Stage | Existing baseline and proposed comparison | Advance only with |
|---|---|---|
| A | Source-only plus each independent teacher using existing producers | Exact source/asset/profile binding and valid complete targets |
| B | Existing same-codec KD; direct/bottleneck/feature/relational alternatives | Compatible signal support and downstream benefit |
| C | Selected complementary teacher fusion | Controlled capacity/context, dropout/missing-teacher checks |
| D | SFT, preference baseline, outcome policy, structured credit | Actual probability/algorithm support and independent reward evidence |
| E | Existing exact gradient replay then targeted mechanistic interventions | Parity, causal controls and equal-budget downstream fidelity |
| F | Existing donor boundary transfer plus bounded edit proposals | Parent preservation, optimizer/rollback compatibility, matched controls |
| G | Selected recipes on a second size and architecture | Actual conformance and unchanged evaluator meaning |

Do not enable all techniques at once. Start with strong current-compatible historical families, not only the early weak baseline. Prioritize the readout-to-generation error, matched exposure/optimizer interactions, and selection frontier before expensive broad circuit analysis.

## 10. Measurement, versioning and reproducibility

Primary endpoint: total cost/time to first evaluation checkpoint satisfying predeclared sustained fidelity, formal-validity and retention requirements. Numeric thresholds, cadence, seeds and budgets must be fixed before comparison. If a method never crosses, report censoring and quality at budget.

Include teacher production, projection fitting, retrieval, sampling, fitting, analysis, verifier calls, failed/rejected proposals, retries and tuning. Separate first-use and amortized costs. Report fixed-compute quality, pass@1 separately from pass@k, memory observations versus enforced limits, and unsupported/abstention rates.

Use source/dependency-grouped splits, multiple seeds and an untouched final population. Repeated development selection does not create new holdout evidence. Preserve all original failures, not only successful arms.

Bind code/config/checkpoint/tokenizer/precision, teacher extraction and compression, populations/interpretations/definitions, retrieval index, loss/reward/credit/intervention versions, optimizer/RNG/replay/curriculum state and local environment/resources. Reject incompatible resume or changed identities rather than silently adopting them.

Source changes can invalidate historical checkpoint manifests even when numerical code appears similar. Existing explicit transitions and frozen projection-only readers do not grant full decoder compatibility.

## 11. Local implementation and validation roadmap

Implement only after existing coordination permits the exact project change and owner workflow:

1. Map additive capability/profile views onto the inspected owners without changing default identities or creating a second registry.
2. Bind an eligible complete-target population and selected current-compatible checkpoint pair; verify actual tokenizer framing/body/EOS capacity and resource/state footprint.
3. Preserve baseline/default behavior and owning tests; qualify refusal paths as well as supported calls.
4. Extend one objective or diagnostic at a time under a separate recipe/event identity.
5. Keep gradient replay and speculative updates private until matched controls and retention support acceptance.
6. Add policy scoring/credit only after the backend's actual action semantics and behavior identities are qualified.
7. Run meaningful existing-owner local tests and admitted numerical comparisons; no hosted Actions, automatic installs, or model downloads.
8. Update the maintained repository guides/catalog in place after receipt-backed changes. Do not copy this planning package into a parallel implementation tree.

Proposed regression designs cover unknown/error labels; shape/pooling/probability mismatches; checkpoint/source drift; target leakage; unsupported capabilities; stale interventions; exact replay and RNG/Adam integrity; rollback; duplicate feedback; same-reward groups; retained rejection dispositions; and semantic failure despite proof success.

