## 623. Use the independent seed and group draws more efficiently

The proposed confidence profile keeps the complete crossed population-fidelity estimand and equal-group missingness bounds. Write the S-by-G table as disjoint matchings. Each matching contains `min(S,G)` cells that share neither a seed draw nor a legal dependency-group draw. The two-sample Hoeffding argument bounds each matching mean. Convexity of the exponential combines the matchings even though they reuse draws across matchings. The resulting two-sided radius is `sqrt(2*log(2/alpha)/min(S,G))`. Apply it to the lower and upper bounds that retain every unknown cell. This derivation assumes a fixed prospective frame, fixed training and review policy, and independent seed and group draws. [Hoeffding, Theorem 2 and Section 5b](https://www.cs.rpi.edu/academics/courses/spring06/random/hoefding.pdf)

